---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Stamp from '../components/Stamp.astro';
import { vendors, priced, money, KLASS_LABEL, PAIRS, pairSlug, bySlug, badge } from '../data/site.js';

const emr = vendors.filter(v => v.klass === 'emr');
const booking = vendors.filter(v => v.klass === 'booking');
const promo = vendors.filter(v => v.promo);
const quoteOnly = vendors.filter(v => !v.pricingPublic);
const cheapest = priced.slice(0, 7);
const featured = PAIRS.slice(0, 3);
---
<Base
  title="MedSpaStack — independent pricing research on med spa software"
  description={`Verified pricing, hidden fees and clinical-capability data for ${vendors.length} med spa and aesthetics platforms. Read from vendor pages, dated, rechecked weekly.`}
>
<section class="ms-section">
  <p class="ms-eyebrow">Independent research</p>
  <h1 class="ms-display">What med spa software actually costs</h1>
  <p class="ms-lede ms-measure">
    We track published pricing, setup fees and add-on charges across {vendors.length} med spa and
    aesthetics platforms — and record which ones have real medical charting versus which are
    booking systems wearing a clinical label. Every number carries the date we read it off the
    vendor's own page.
  </p>
  <Stamp />
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <div class="ms-stats blueprint">
    <i class="corner tl"></i><i class="corner tr"></i><i class="corner bl"></i><i class="corner br"></i>
    <div class="ms-stat">
      <div class="ms-stat-fig">{vendors.length}</div>
      <p class="ms-stat-cap">Platforms tracked, rechecked weekly</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ms-stat">
      <div class="ms-stat-fig">{priced.length}</div>
      <p class="ms-stat-cap">Publish a price at all — the other {quoteOnly.length} quote only</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ms-stat">
      <div class="ms-stat-fig">{emr.length}</div>
      <p class="ms-stat-cap">Have real medical charting, not a booking system with a clinical label</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ms-stat">
      <div class="ms-stat-fig">{promo.length}</div>
      <p class="ms-stat-cap">Quote a promotional or annual-prepay rate as if it were standard</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <div class="ms-callout ms-callout-accent">
    <p class="ms-callout-title">Why this site exists</p>
    <p>
      Advertised starting prices in this category are close to meaningless. Several platforms bill
      per location or per user rather than per business, {promo.length} quote a promotional or
      annual-prepay rate as if it were standard, and nearly every one charges separately for the
      things a med spa actually needs — charting, e-prescribing, forms, marketing. We publish the
      whole bill, not the headline.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <p class="ms-kicker">Lowest published starting prices</p>
  <h2 class="ms-h2">Sticker prices, and what they leave out</h2>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    Sorted by advertised entry price. Read the billing basis before drawing conclusions — several
    of these are per user or per location, which changes the arithmetic entirely once you have a
    team.
  </p>

  <div class="ms-scroller">
    <table class="ms-data ms-data-sticky">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Platform</th>
          <th scope="col">Type</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">From</th>
          <th scope="col">Billing basis</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Setup</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {cheapest.map(v => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class="ms-cell-name"><a href={`/software/${v.slug}/`}>{v.displayName}</a></span>
              {v.promo && <span class="ms-cell-flags"><span class="ms-badge ms-badge-promo">Promo rate</span></span>}
            </td>
            <td><span class={badge(v.klass)}>{KLASS_LABEL[v.klass]}</span></td>
            <td class="num num-strong">{money(v.startingPrice)}/mo</td>
            <td class="prose">{(v.entryNote || '—').split(';')[0]}</td>
            <td class="num">{v.setupFee ? money(v.setupFee) : <span class="nil">—</span>}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="ms-scrollnote">Showing {cheapest.length} of {vendors.length}. <a href="/pricing/">See the full pricing database →</a></p>
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <p class="ms-kicker">Start here</p>
  <h2 class="ms-h2">Three things worth knowing before you shortlist</h2>
  <div class="ms-grid">
    <a class="ms-linkcard" href="/emr-vs-booking/">
      <span class="ms-linkcard-title">Booking system or EMR?</span>
      <p class="ms-linkcard-desc">
        {emr.length} of these platforms have genuine medical charting. {booking.length} have none at
        all. Buying across that line is how practices end up paying for two systems.
      </p>
      <span class="ms-linkcard-meta">Guide</span>
    </a>
    <a class="ms-linkcard" href="/pricing/">
      <span class="ms-linkcard-title">The pricing database</span>
      <p class="ms-linkcard-desc">
        Every published tier, onboarding fee and add-on charge for all {vendors.length} platforms,
        with the source and date for each.
      </p>
      <span class="ms-linkcard-meta">Data</span>
    </a>
    <a class="ms-linkcard" href="/cost-calculator/">
      <span class="ms-linkcard-title">What will it cost you?</span>
      <p class="ms-linkcard-desc">
        Per-location and per-user pricing converted onto one basis for your practice shape, with
        onboarding folded into year one.
      </p>
      <span class="ms-linkcard-meta">Tool</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <p class="ms-kicker">Head to head</p>
  <h2 class="ms-h2">Recent comparisons</h2>
  <div class="ms-grid">
    {featured.map(p => {
      const a = bySlug[p[0]], b = bySlug[p[1]];
      return a && b && (
        <a class="ms-linkcard" href={`/compare/${pairSlug(p)}/`}>
          <span class="ms-linkcard-title">{a.displayName} vs {b.displayName}</span>
          <p class="ms-linkcard-desc">
            {a.pricingPublic !== b.pricingPublic
              ? 'One publishes a price and the other does not — what that asymmetry costs you in a buying cycle.'
              : 'Published pricing, billing basis and clinical capability, side by side.'}
          </p>
          <span class="ms-linkcard-meta">Comparison</span>
        </a>
      );
    })}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <p class="ms-kicker">The three most expensive assumptions</p>

  <h3 class="ms-h3">1. That the advertised price is per business</h3>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    It usually is not. Boulevard, Mangomint, Mindbody and Square Appointments price
    <em>per location</em>. Aesthetic Record and Fresha price <em>per user</em> — Aesthetic Record's
    $15 entry tier becomes $90 a month for a six-person clinic before a single add-on, and it
    carries a $399 onboarding fee that appears nowhere near the headline. Two platforms with
    similar sticker prices can differ threefold on the invoice.
  </p>

  <h3 class="ms-h3">2. That clinical charting is included</h3>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    Fresha, Vagaro, Square Appointments, WellnessLiving, Mindbody and Booker have no medical
    charting at all. They are excellent booking systems. If you inject, laser or prescribe, you
    will be buying a second system — a cost that rarely appears in any comparison table.
    <a href="/emr-vs-booking/">We sorted every platform on this axis.</a>
  </p>

  <h3 class="ms-h3">3. That the annual price is the price</h3>
  <p class="ms-measure">
    Most published rates here assume annual prepayment, and several are promotional. Boulevard's
    listed $140 tier is a summer promotion against a $176 standard rate, on annual billing, per
    location. We record the standard rate alongside the promotional one.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="ms-section">
  <div class="ms-callout">
    <p class="ms-callout-title">Corrections</p>
    <p>
      Vendors change prices without notice, and a stale figure is worse than no figure. If what you
      were quoted differs from what we publish, that is a defect on our side —
      <a href="/about/">send it over</a> and we will re-read the source and republish with a new
      verification date.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
